author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Transport accepts current subscription types and always attempts unsubscribe_events cleanup; Entity delta command supports entity ID and domain filters, bounded duration/count, initial snapshot inclusion control, and normalized deterministic envelopes; Automation platforms command supports trigger and condition catalogs and stable bounded output; Help, schema, README/docs, unit/integration/live tests, all formats, source docs, file size, duplication, security, package, and release gates pass"
definition_of_ready: Tagged Core 2026.7.4 schemas and live 2026.7.4 behavior are known; existing subscription transport and tests inspected
goal: agent-native-home-state-observation
objective: implement-typed-delta-platform-contracts
value: Avoid repeated full state polling and raw protocol parsing for agent workflows.
impact: "Efficient, bounded monitoring and automation authoring discovery become first-class CLI capabilities."
outcome: "Typed source, tests, docs, and live proof integrated into the hassio command surface."
why_now: The CLI supports generic WebSocket calls but not the current optimized subscriptions needed by agents.
parent: hac-usxc
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: api-parity-2026-07
release: unreleased
resolution: Implemented and verified the typed WebSocket subscriptions and agent-oriented CLI contracts.
expected_result: "Home Assistant entity and automation discovery is bounded, typed, documented, format-safe, and fully tested."
actual_result: All implementation acceptance criteria passed locally and through PM-linked test execution.
