comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:22.979Z",codex-root,Command design will follow current Core source while keeping the raw call command as the forward-compatibility escape hatch.
  "2026-07-31T20:31:51.763Z",codex-root,"Live built CLI on Home Assistant 2026.7.4 validated automation platform catalogs and compact entity observation. Evidence retains only version, catalog counts, and field shapes; no entity identifiers, state values, credentials, or topology were stored."
  "2026-07-31T20:37:43.405Z",codex-root,Live read-only built-CLI acceptance passed against Home Assistant Core 2026.7.4 across TOON JSON compact JSON YAML table and Markdown. Entity output was inspected only for counts and field shape; no private URL token entity IDs states or payloads were persisted.
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:22.979Z",codex-root,"Live acceptance records only version, counts, and schema shapes; entity IDs and state values remain private."
  "2026-07-31T20:31:50.970Z",codex-root,"Measured full Vitest coverage after transport, command, capability, and documentation integration: 1,294 tests and exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions, and lines."
  "2026-07-31T20:37:43.405Z",codex-root,Trivy initially could not allocate its download beneath the quota-exhausted host /tmp. The same mandatory scan passed with an isolated TMPDIR and reported zero HIGH or CRITICAL vulnerabilities misconfigurations or secrets.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:22.979Z",codex-root,"subscribe_entities emits compact add/change/remove deltas rather than state_changed event objects, so its normalization must be protocol-specific."
